{"name":"River Rouge","hex":"#ec9b9d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"river","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large and often winding stream which drains a land mass, carrying water down from higher areas to a lower point, oftentimes ending in another body of water, such as an ocean or in an inland sea.","Any large flow of a liquid in a single body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To improve one’s hand to beat another player on the final card in a poker game."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river"},{"term":"rouge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish pink colour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Red or pink makeup to add colour to the cheeks; blusher.","Any reddish pink colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rouge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rouge River (Ontario)","blocks":[{"text":"The Rouge River is a river in Markham, Pickering, Richmond Hill and Toronto in the Greater Toronto Area of Ontario, Canada. The river flows from the Oak Ridges Moraine to Lake Ontario at the eastern border of Toronto, and is the location of Rouge Park, the only national park in Canada within a municipality. At its southern end, the Rouge River is the boundary between Toronto and southwestern Pickering in the Regional Municipality of Durham."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Finch_Meandor_with_Rouge_River.jpg/330px-Finch_Meandor_with_Rouge_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rouge_River_(Ontario)","wikidata":"Q2169206"},{"title":"Scarborough—Rouge River (federal electoral district)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarborough—Rouge River was a federal electoral district in Ontario, Canada, that has been represented in the House of Commons of Canada between 1988 and 2015. However, as of the Fall 2015 federal election, part of this riding has been combined with the south-western part of the old riding Pickering—Scarborough East."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Scarborough_Rouge_River.png/330px-Scarborough_Rouge_River.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarborough%E2%80%94Rouge_River_(federal_electoral_district)","wikidata":"Q3475170"},{"title":"River Rouge (Michigan)","blocks":[{"text":"The River Rouge is a 127-mile (204 km) river in the Metro Detroit area of southeastern Michigan. It flows into the Detroit River at Zug Island, which is the boundary between the cities of River Rouge and Detroit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/River_rouge_falls.jpg/330px-River_rouge_falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Rouge_(Michigan)","wikidata":"Q447316"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River","wikidata":"Q4022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lower_course_of_the_Rouge_River%2C_circa_1932.jpg/500px-Lower_course_of_the_Rouge_River%2C_circa_1932.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lower_course_of_the_Rouge_River%2C_circa_1932.jpg/1280px-Lower_course_of_the_Rouge_River%2C_circa_1932.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lower_course_of_the_Rouge_River%2C_circa_1932.jpg/500px-Lower_course_of_the_Rouge_River%2C_circa_1932.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lower course of the Rouge River, circa 1932","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALower_course_of_the_Rouge_River%2C_circa_1932.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Rouge_River_Marshes.jpg/500px-Rouge_River_Marshes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Rouge_River_Marshes.jpg/1280px-Rouge_River_Marshes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Rouge_River_Marshes.jpg/500px-Rouge_River_Marshes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marshes located near the estuary","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARouge_River_Marshes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Estuary_of_the_Rouge.jpg/500px-Estuary_of_the_Rouge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Estuary_of_the_Rouge.jpg/1280px-Estuary_of_the_Rouge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Estuary_of_the_Rouge.jpg/500px-Estuary_of_the_Rouge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&